## Recovery objectives

For the current static marketing site, target a four-hour recovery time and 24-hour recovery point for repository and configuration evidence. These are objectives, not measured guarantees.

## Recovery order

1. secure GitHub, Cloudflare, domain, Turnstile, and email-provider accounts;
2. restore the canonical repository and verify commit signatures or hashes where available;
3. restore environment configuration from the approved private inventory;
4. deploy the last known-good tested archive;
5. verify DNS, TLS, headers, primary pages, and safe contact behavior;
6. rebuild only after service is stable and dependencies are reviewed;
7. reconcile Markdoc current-state pages and incident evidence.

## Required offline knowledge

Maintain private recovery contacts, account ownership, domain registrar access, token rotation procedure, Cloudflare account and zone identifiers, last known-good commit and digest, and billing recovery. Do not commit that confidential inventory here.

## Test

Perform a tabletop every six months and a non-production restoration annually. Record time, missing access, unclear steps, and follow-up owners.
